    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=191fb38a-3b70-4f49-b37f-cb2eda186474&ccId=9201943470232_2&jobId=9202002440927_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Teacher Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Bellevue\n\nPosition Summary Bellevue University seeks a dedicated and collaborative Assistant Professor to join its Teacher Education program. This is a full-time, at-will faculty position with primary responsibilities in teaching, student engagement, and service to the program, university, and profession. The standard teaching load for this position is eight (8) courses per academic year, with additional expectations for service and participation in program development and continuous improvement.   Essential Duties and Responsibilities   Teaching and Instruction Teach undergraduate-level courses consistent with assigned workload (8 courses per academic year). Deliver instruction aligned with approved curriculum, and course objectives. Employ inclusive, evidence-informed, and engaging instructional strategies appropriate for teacher education. Integrate theory, research, policy, and practice across the curriculum. Assess student learning using established assignments, rubrics, and grading standards. Provide timely, constructive, and developmentally appropriate feedback to students. Maintain accurate academic records and meet all grading and reporting deadlines. Teach in online, hybrid, or on-ground formats, as determined by program needs.   Program and University Service Participation in program meetings, committees, and curriculum development initiatives. Contribution to program assessment, accreditation-related activities, and continuous quality improvement. Engagement in student advising, mentoring, and support as assigned. Participation in university service activities, including committees, task forces, or faculty governance. Collaboration with colleagues to support program growth, innovation, and mission alignment. Professional Engagement Maintain professional competence and knowledge of current trends in teacher education and practice. Uphold Bellevue University policies. Engage in ongoing professional development, scholarship, or practice-related activities consistent with the role.   Required Qualifications Master’s Degree in Teacher Education is required.  At least 3-5 years of teaching experience in the education field at the K-12 level. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Strong interest in or experience with first-generation, first-year, and at-risk students is a plus.  Experience in curriculum design is desired. A commitment to the development and delivery of online and/or hybrid courses is highly desirable. Effective communication skills, including verbal and written communication. Ability to exercise sound judgment in establishing and maintaining effective working relationships with fellow employees, the University community, and the public in general.   Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in Education (EdD or PhD). Prior teaching experience teaching in a Teacher Education program Experience in areas aligned with program needs (elementary education, special education, ESL, and STEM) Prior field experience coordination Experience with curriculum development, assessment, and/or accreditation processes   Workload and Appointment Terms Full-time, at-will faculty appointment Teaching load of nine (8) courses per academic year Additional responsibilities include program, university, and professional service Workload distribution may vary by term based on program needs   Pay and Benefits The yearly salary for this role ranges from $65,000 - $80,000 Bellevue University full-time faculty enjoy an excellent benefits package which include: medical, dental, vision, life, disability, 403(b) retirement and tuition remission.   Information Needed to Apply Cover letter addressing how qualifications match position requirements. Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Names and contact information for three professional references. NOTE: The statements above are intended to describe the general nature and level of work involved for this job. It is not an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required of this job. This document does not create an employment contract, implied or otherwise, other than an “at will” relationship. The Higher Education Opportunity Act requires institutions participating in federally funded financial aid programs to make information about the institution available to the public, current and prospective students, and current and prospective employees. The Bellevue University Consumer Information webpage, found at  www.bellevue.edu/student-support/consumer-information/consumer-information , provides readily accessible information to help consumers make informed decisions about post-secondary education. Bellevue University’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASR), found at  www.bellevue.edu/student-support/consumer-information/pdfs/annual-safety-report.pdf , provides information about campus crime statistics and institutional security policies and procedures as well as information about student housing fire statistics and fire safety policies. You can obtain a paper copy of these reports from the Bellevue Dean of Students office by calling 402-557-7028. In addition to this, Bellevue University is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .",
